WEBVTT

00:01.750 --> 00:03.830
We are Amarariruku.

00:04.560 --> 00:06.290
"The ones who dream."

00:07.270 --> 00:09.230
We'll see each other again soon.

00:11.130 --> 00:15.110
To think that Stigma was 
building up his own forces...

00:15.290 --> 00:17.990
He said they were called "Amarariruku."

00:18.450 --> 00:23.580
The girl we fought was able to 
control ice even without the ring.

00:24.000 --> 00:29.090
I'm sure they wanted to see if 
those powers worked against heroes.

00:29.650 --> 00:30.960
See if they'd work?

00:32.980 --> 00:36.270
If only I had realized this was their trap...

00:37.650 --> 00:40.890
I am... truly sorry.

00:41.130 --> 00:44.770
N-No, no! You shouldn't have 
to apologize, Unilord-san!

00:45.720 --> 00:46.630
Yes?

00:46.630 --> 00:47.940
<i>This is Lady Black.</i>

00:48.240 --> 00:50.150
<i>I'm done treating Spirit.</i>

00:50.150 --> 00:52.560
Oh, okay! I'll be right there!

00:53.330 --> 00:55.910
<i>Someone who can use powers 
without the ring...</i>

00:56.410 --> 00:59.430
<i>This could be headed in the 
worst possible direction.</i>

02:33.130 --> 02:38.090
<b><u>Episode 7
</u>Unchain</b>

02:42.320 --> 02:44.550
Pepesha-san, are you okay?

02:44.550 --> 02:45.510
Teru-chan!

02:45.880 --> 02:47.870
I'm fine! This is nothing.

02:48.270 --> 02:51.350
I just had a little hole in my stomach.

02:52.440 --> 02:53.520
<i>"Little"?</i>

02:53.520 --> 02:56.900
A puncture wound, hypothermia, 
and a decent amount of bleeding.

02:56.900 --> 02:59.010
You're not fine at all!

02:59.010 --> 03:00.810
The bigger problem is that

03:00.810 --> 03:04.120
their attacks can actually damage
us even in our Heart-shift forms.

03:04.410 --> 03:07.150
What the heck is their deal?

03:08.570 --> 03:12.370
That girl... She called me "Pesha."

03:14.620 --> 03:19.630
Only those who are 
closest to me call me Pesha.

03:19.910 --> 03:21.020
Does that mean...

03:21.020 --> 03:23.560
You mean she knows you, Pepesha-san?

03:23.560 --> 03:25.350
It's likely.

03:25.890 --> 03:29.340
But... I don't know who she is.

03:30.920 --> 03:32.350
I wonder why...

03:34.230 --> 03:36.190
I have a really bad feeling about this.

03:37.180 --> 03:39.940
It's like an old wound 
that started to hurt again...

03:40.540 --> 03:41.710
Some kind of loathing.

03:45.470 --> 03:47.660
P-Pepesha-san! You should rest!

03:48.130 --> 03:49.520
No, I'm fine.

03:50.140 --> 03:51.160
More importantly...

03:51.580 --> 03:52.790
They...

03:53.140 --> 03:54.760
Amarariruku...

03:54.760 --> 03:57.610
As far as I could tell, 
they were all children.

03:58.320 --> 03:59.760
Now that you mention it...

03:59.760 --> 04:00.670
Children...

04:01.540 --> 04:05.800
With names like Amarariruku and Weepy...

04:06.560 --> 04:09.600
They're all very childish names.

04:11.150 --> 04:14.620
I wonder if maybe Stigma is 
just playing in this world...

04:15.750 --> 04:18.620
like a child.

04:23.360 --> 04:26.690
It's far too early to determine that.

04:26.690 --> 04:31.120
If we miscalculate their motives, it will 
put us at an even bigger disadvantage.

04:31.380 --> 04:34.180
Yes... You're exactly right.

04:34.180 --> 04:36.460
But Stigma is elusive.

04:37.260 --> 04:39.670
What exactly can we do?

04:40.650 --> 04:44.970
It seems that it's necessary for us to 
learn more about just who Stigma is.

04:46.140 --> 04:47.520
Bring her here.

04:47.520 --> 04:48.400
"Her"?

04:48.400 --> 04:50.470
Um... Is someone coming?

04:50.790 --> 04:53.830
She is our new hope.

04:56.080 --> 04:57.330
Shrimpy-san?

04:58.470 --> 04:59.230
Is this it?

04:59.620 --> 05:01.690
Ko... Koishikawa-san!

05:01.690 --> 05:03.240
What are you doing here?

05:04.820 --> 05:06.850
Momijiyama-san! Thank goodness!

05:06.850 --> 05:08.760
I heard you had an awful time!

05:08.760 --> 05:09.930
Are you okay?

05:09.930 --> 05:11.830
I, um... yes.

05:12.300 --> 05:15.230
Unilord... By "hope," you don't mean...

05:15.230 --> 05:17.880
I called her here myself.

05:17.880 --> 05:19.620
You did?

05:19.620 --> 05:20.440
Yes.

05:20.440 --> 05:22.470
With this super-cheap smartphone.

05:23.240 --> 05:26.240
At this moment, she is the only 
thing Stigma won't predict.

05:26.700 --> 05:32.470
She is an unknown factor 
to both ourselves and Stigma.

05:36.990 --> 05:40.160
There is something that 
I must report to all of you.

05:40.160 --> 05:42.820
It's regarding the ring.

05:43.030 --> 05:47.030
The ring... The one that put 
Koishikawa-san through hell?

05:47.430 --> 05:50.700
Yes. Our analysis of that 
ring has progressed,

05:51.190 --> 05:53.660
and we've discovered a number of things.

05:54.200 --> 05:55.910
The reason she was invited here

05:55.910 --> 05:59.170
was because we had to explain 
something regarding the ring.

05:59.370 --> 06:05.110
This ring is a frightful thing that is 
actually Stigma's heart materialized.

06:05.920 --> 06:07.610
His heart?

06:11.840 --> 06:16.520
Within everyone's heart is 
their own unique wavelength.

06:16.520 --> 06:18.310
Their own way of being.

06:20.650 --> 06:25.780
That ring takes the wearer's heart 
and connects it to Stigma's heart.

06:26.040 --> 06:30.490
It then changes that heart's way of 
being. Truly, a terrifying thing.

06:32.300 --> 06:36.170
Then... The reason Koishikawa-san 
turned into that thing...

06:36.170 --> 06:38.330
And the incident that 
happened in my country...

06:38.800 --> 06:45.340
Yes. So it can be said that he is spreading 
parts of his heart all over the world.

06:46.700 --> 06:50.110
There's actually something 
I remember after hearing this.

06:50.740 --> 06:54.360
That day, when Momijiyama-san saved me...

06:54.360 --> 06:58.100
My memories of fighting 
her aren't very clear...

06:59.510 --> 07:03.310
But I have clear memories of something else.

07:06.300 --> 07:09.850
At the same time that my 
own darkness came out,

07:09.850 --> 07:13.780
my consciousness sank deep into my heart.

07:15.360 --> 07:16.860
A huge chasm...

07:17.480 --> 07:20.040
No, I guess I should call it a wound.

07:20.890 --> 07:23.760
I think it was a wound within a heart.

07:24.660 --> 07:30.340
Thinking back on it now, I think what was 
deep within that wound was Stigma's heart.

07:33.670 --> 07:37.510
Does that mean you personally 
saw Stigma's heart, Iko-chan?

07:37.840 --> 07:40.540
I'm pretty sure every 
other one of Stigma's victims

07:40.540 --> 07:43.210
didn't have any recollection 
of what happened.

07:43.210 --> 07:45.520
And that's why we were unable to notice

07:45.840 --> 07:51.280
the possibility that the ring connected 
the wearer's heart with Stigma's heart.

07:51.600 --> 07:54.000
Seriously, what is Stigma's deal?

07:54.000 --> 07:56.600
Is he trying to turn strangers into... himself?

07:56.600 --> 07:57.780
Back then...

07:58.410 --> 08:00.780
When I saw Stigma's heart...

08:00.780 --> 08:04.490
The way he saw the world 
and what he desired...

08:04.950 --> 08:08.220
A part of that vision flowed into me.

08:09.210 --> 08:09.980
Huh?

08:09.980 --> 08:11.760
Tell us, Iko-chan.

08:11.760 --> 08:14.220
I want to know whatever I can about his goal.

08:15.000 --> 08:20.220
The heart I saw... was very abstract.

08:20.950 --> 08:23.130
I'm pretty sure that was Earth...

08:23.650 --> 08:27.230
People's shadows were hand in hand, 
and they created a ring.

08:28.240 --> 08:30.910
I think that's Stigma's ideal.

08:30.910 --> 08:34.880
People hand in hand and 
becoming one upon this planet.

08:34.880 --> 08:36.280
Becoming one?

08:37.090 --> 08:40.290
N-Now, hang on a sec! 
That almost sounds like...

08:40.290 --> 08:41.440
Yes.

08:42.020 --> 08:44.790
I can't say I agree with this, but...

08:48.840 --> 08:53.220
World peace. I believe that's his goal.

08:53.630 --> 08:54.720
What?!

08:55.100 --> 08:57.510
He wants world peace after 
causing that whole mess?!

08:57.510 --> 08:59.470
Bring that guy here this instant!

08:58.520 --> 08:59.470
Now, now...

08:59.470 --> 09:02.470
<b>Badump Badump</b>

09:00.000 --> 09:02.470
This wouldn't be so troublesome 
if we could do that.

09:03.370 --> 09:05.390
A-And one other thing...

09:05.740 --> 09:08.400
The inside of Stigma's heart...

09:12.200 --> 09:14.840
seemed extremely childlike.

09:15.920 --> 09:19.940
Very young, almost like 
he was refusing to grow up.

09:21.440 --> 09:22.730
A child...

09:22.730 --> 09:23.750
So basically,

09:24.150 --> 09:28.750
he's a little brat who thinks his 
actions will lead to world peace.

09:29.070 --> 09:31.020
P-Pretty much.

09:31.020 --> 09:34.710
That's about all I got from Stigma's heart.

09:34.710 --> 09:36.590
Is that helpful at all?

09:36.910 --> 09:38.930
Of course it is, Iko-san.

09:38.930 --> 09:44.600
Being able to see even a fragment of 
Stigma's vision will help us read his next move.

09:45.040 --> 09:46.400
Thank goodness.

09:46.400 --> 09:48.850
Um, thank you very much.

09:49.160 --> 09:51.590
That must have been so hard for you.

09:51.590 --> 09:53.360
No, it's fine.

09:53.900 --> 09:58.720
I'm the one who said I wanted 
to tell all of you this, anyway.

09:58.720 --> 09:59.360
Huh?

10:00.330 --> 10:01.990
I've been thinking this whole time...

10:02.510 --> 10:05.470
How can I be of some help to you?

10:06.600 --> 10:09.390
But I'm just a regular person.

10:09.390 --> 10:13.340
Even if I wanted to fight with you, 
I'd just be in the way.

10:15.110 --> 10:17.220
So was I at least a little useful?

10:17.520 --> 10:20.440
I mean... You don't have to ask that.

10:21.830 --> 10:25.430
Unilord, there's one other 
thing that's come to my mind.

10:25.760 --> 10:28.940
The girl named Tzveta that we 
ran into at the North Pole...

10:31.200 --> 10:35.570
I have a feeling she looks a lot 
like I did when I was a child.

10:36.380 --> 10:37.940
What do you mean?

10:38.310 --> 10:40.460
I'm not sure, but...

10:40.920 --> 10:43.730
The déjà vu and loathing I felt from her...

10:44.220 --> 10:46.730
It felt a lot like me.

10:48.670 --> 10:49.670
Pepesha-san?!

10:49.670 --> 10:50.810
Pepesha-san?!

10:52.490 --> 10:53.630
Are you okay?

10:53.960 --> 10:57.090
A wound that deep isn't going 
to fully heal right away.

10:57.090 --> 10:59.300
You should go home for 
today and get some rest.

10:59.570 --> 11:02.420
Yeah... I think I will.

11:04.040 --> 11:06.680
Once I recover, I'll do some 
investigating back home...

11:07.170 --> 11:08.670
on myself.

11:08.670 --> 11:12.690
All right. But for now, please 
concentrate on your recovery.

11:13.740 --> 11:15.440
Will you be all right by yourself?

11:15.870 --> 11:18.280
I'm fine. Thanks.

11:28.230 --> 11:29.710
Pepesha-san!

11:30.490 --> 11:31.460
Teru-chan?

11:31.940 --> 11:34.090
What's the matter? Where's Iko-chan?

11:34.090 --> 11:37.020
Koishikawa-san went home already.

11:37.020 --> 11:40.220
But I wanted to talk to you, Pepesha-san.

11:40.530 --> 11:41.630
About what?

11:41.630 --> 11:42.520
Um...

11:44.490 --> 11:48.060
It just seemed like you were depressed.

11:49.040 --> 11:50.980
That's not true at all.

11:51.200 --> 11:53.090
See? Perfectly fine!

11:54.960 --> 11:55.770
No?

11:56.940 --> 12:00.990
Well... honestly, I don't really get it myself.

12:02.370 --> 12:07.080
Even if the girl we met at the 
North Pole is someone I know,

12:07.080 --> 12:09.240
she's being used by someone else,

12:09.880 --> 12:12.130
and I wasn't able to do anything about it.

12:13.500 --> 12:16.750
I think... that was a bit shocking to me.

12:16.750 --> 12:18.900
But... that's not true.

12:19.730 --> 12:21.630
This isn't your fault!

12:24.890 --> 12:25.760
Huh?

12:26.980 --> 12:27.470
Huh?!

12:27.770 --> 12:30.030
Wh-Wh-What?!

12:31.520 --> 12:35.230
Why are you looking so glum, Teru-chan?

12:35.440 --> 12:38.170
Oh, I guess that's my fault. Sorry about that.

12:39.210 --> 12:42.110
Man, I could really use a drink right now.

12:42.570 --> 12:45.610
But I guess I'll have to hold 
off for a while until I recover.

12:45.860 --> 12:47.840
P-Please don't tease me like that!

12:47.840 --> 12:50.870
I just want to help you out, Pepesha-san...

12:51.200 --> 12:52.530
I...

12:55.420 --> 12:57.850
Thank you for worrying about me.

12:57.850 --> 13:01.380
But Teru-chan, I'm gonna let you 
in on something very important.

13:01.760 --> 13:03.740
When you want to cheer someone up,

13:03.740 --> 13:06.300
you need to smile to tell 
them everything will be okay.

13:07.470 --> 13:09.050
Well, see you later!

13:11.490 --> 13:12.580
Pepesha-san!

13:14.560 --> 13:16.320
You said before...

13:17.040 --> 13:21.980
"Carry with you all the brilliance you 
weren't able to save, and move forward."

13:23.680 --> 13:27.030
Right now, I have the courage to carry that.

13:27.030 --> 13:28.110
It'll be okay.

13:28.680 --> 13:32.720
If we carry this together, 
we'll be able to save that girl!

13:33.240 --> 13:34.400
Teru-chan...

13:35.370 --> 13:40.630
There you go, using what you just 
learned in real time. You're so cute.

13:40.870 --> 13:45.880
Y-Yes! That's right! I-I can do 
things when they really matter!

13:47.200 --> 13:48.830
But yeah...

13:48.830 --> 13:52.650
I guess I need to be able to actually 
do the things I told you to do.

13:53.880 --> 13:55.020
In that case...

13:55.400 --> 13:57.620
Will you carry this with me,

13:58.740 --> 13:59.540
Shy?

14:03.320 --> 14:06.030
Of course, Spirit!

14:09.370 --> 14:11.200
Looks like they'll be okay.

14:11.730 --> 14:13.950
Well, she's not that weak.

14:15.030 --> 14:16.220
Neither of them are.

14:21.700 --> 14:22.540
Shy.

14:24.590 --> 14:28.010
None

14:24.590 --> 14:28.010
25 years since birth

14:24.590 --> 14:28.010
<u>N. Vilio 
Nationality: Spaceship 
 Likes: The people close to him, taking 
care of others, bad puns
Shy's partner. Many other units
 have the same form as him.</u>

14:31.370 --> 14:33.510
There's no need for revolution!

14:33.510 --> 14:38.020
<b>Revolution</b>

14:33.910 --> 14:38.020
All this world needs is absolute order!

14:38.020 --> 14:44.150
Order of the presidents, by the 
presidents, for the presidents!

14:44.450 --> 14:47.400
It's over, revolutionary fighters!

14:47.940 --> 14:50.320
Stand up! Stand up, everyone!

14:52.240 --> 14:55.240
The world doesn't just belong to you!

14:57.660 --> 15:00.420
Say your prayers, Evil President!

15:01.310 --> 15:02.670
I'll defeat you!

15:03.150 --> 15:07.670
I'm the warrior with the 
fiery soul... R-Revozeale...

15:08.960 --> 15:09.930
It's Zeale.

15:10.480 --> 15:11.420
Who's that?

15:11.420 --> 15:12.430
Isn't that Shy?

15:14.290 --> 15:16.050
<i>Please just kill me right now.</i>

15:17.200 --> 15:21.200
<i>This happened a few days after 
the incident at the North Pole,</i>

15:21.200 --> 15:24.100
<i>while Pepesha-san was still recovering.</i>

15:25.350 --> 15:27.900
Another stage performance request?

15:28.200 --> 15:33.530
Yeah. It seems that after the fire incident, 
your popularity is going up a little.

15:33.820 --> 15:36.440
C-Can we decline that request?

15:36.440 --> 15:40.040
I really don't like talking 
in front of people.

15:40.560 --> 15:42.340
I totally understand,

15:42.340 --> 15:46.150
but building up your image is 
another important part of being a hero.

15:46.150 --> 15:49.600
Your popularity's going up, 
so let's take advantage of that.

15:49.600 --> 15:50.550
But...

15:50.940 --> 15:55.350
And I hear there's a special reward 
waiting for you if you accept this request.

15:56.230 --> 15:57.350
Reward?

15:57.350 --> 15:59.810
Natto

15:59.520 --> 16:03.350
<i>No, no, no! A hero can't 
be tempted by such things!</i>

16:03.350 --> 16:05.800
<i>But my reward...</i>

16:05.800 --> 16:06.630
Teru?

16:08.660 --> 16:11.360
I guess you should always 
try everything once...

16:11.720 --> 16:12.650
All right!

16:13.550 --> 16:15.870
Um... What is this?

16:16.220 --> 16:19.220
Wow! I knew you'd look perfect in that!

16:18.620 --> 16:21.160
<b>Rebel!
Civil Revolution</b>

16:18.620 --> 16:21.160
On TV every Sunday
 morning at 9AM!

16:19.220 --> 16:21.160
<i>Rebel! Civil Revolution!</i>

16:21.660 --> 16:26.170
A super popular anime where revolutionary 
warriors fight to defeat the Evil President!

16:26.170 --> 16:28.670
<b>Civil Revolution</b>

16:26.170 --> 16:28.670
On TV every Sunday
 morning at 9 AM!

16:26.550 --> 16:28.670
This is the series' 30th anniversary.

16:29.020 --> 16:33.130
This is the fiery warrior who shows 
up in the latest series, Revozeale!

16:33.520 --> 16:36.010
She looks just like you, Shy-san!

16:36.010 --> 16:38.810
She's super energetic, passionate, 
and loves to stand out!

16:38.810 --> 16:42.890
She's a super strong tomboy 
who has a lot of friends!

16:43.270 --> 16:46.150
<i>Oh, no. We're nothing alike.</i>

16:46.340 --> 16:49.700
I've been curious about 
you for a while, Shy-san!

16:49.700 --> 16:52.570
When I first saw you, I thought 
you were IRL <i>Civirevo</i>!

16:54.300 --> 16:56.160
<i>So now...</i>

16:56.160 --> 16:59.660
Civirevo Special
 Corner

16:56.480 --> 16:59.660
<i>I'm in the middle of a revolution 
at a department store...</i>

16:59.980 --> 17:02.970
What does this have to do with being a hero?

17:02.970 --> 17:05.360
It's important to be popular with the kids.

17:05.360 --> 17:07.670
The one who's popular is Revozeale.

17:08.000 --> 17:10.670
Shrimpy-san, why are you dressed like that?

17:10.670 --> 17:12.870
I'm Revoron! Am I cute?

17:12.870 --> 17:13.530
Uh...

17:14.100 --> 17:15.010
Sure.

17:15.360 --> 17:18.110
Hey, hey! Great job over here!

17:19.110 --> 17:21.840
Thanks to you, the Zeale 
Sword is super popular!

17:21.840 --> 17:24.020
Oh, it is?

17:24.380 --> 17:27.400
And so... I'm sorry to ask 
this out of the blue, but...

17:27.760 --> 17:28.380
Yes?

17:28.380 --> 17:29.820
<i>I have a bad feeling about this...</i>

17:30.150 --> 17:33.400
<b>Civirevo 30th Anniversary Special Event
Shy-san Talk Show</b>

17:31.240 --> 17:33.400
Hello, everyone!

17:34.060 --> 17:36.070
Hello!

17:36.560 --> 17:39.410
<i>See? I knew this was going to happen.</i>

17:39.990 --> 17:43.390
<i>Everyone thinks all heroes 
are weird and love to stand out,</i>

17:43.390 --> 17:45.910
<i>so they think they can do anything to us.</i>

17:46.410 --> 17:50.590
Now, who has a question for Shy?

17:51.000 --> 17:53.740
<i>None of these kids are interested in me...</i>

17:54.090 --> 17:56.020
Me! Me!

17:56.020 --> 17:57.590
Okay, how about you, little girl?

17:58.400 --> 18:04.100
Um, uh... What kind of food do you like, Shy?

18:04.440 --> 18:07.140
Oh, what a cute question!

18:07.140 --> 18:08.600
What's your favorite food?

18:09.200 --> 18:13.360
M-My favorite food... I-I think natto.

18:13.580 --> 18:15.980
<i>H-Huh? This is actually...</i>

18:15.980 --> 18:17.860
Anyone else have any questions?

18:18.130 --> 18:20.410
Do you like <i>Civirevo</i>, too, Shy-san?

18:20.730 --> 18:25.910
Um... I really liked <i>Solo 
Civirevo</i> a few series back.

18:26.320 --> 18:28.370
Is it hard being a hero?

18:28.620 --> 18:31.880
I-It is hard, but it's also very worthwhile.

18:32.250 --> 18:35.110
Do you hang out with the other heroes?

18:35.110 --> 18:37.590
I wouldn't say we hang out...

18:37.590 --> 18:42.230
But I talk to them at times, and 
sometimes we go on missions together!

18:42.230 --> 18:46.700
<i>Did... people always seem 
this interested in me?</i>

18:43.850 --> 18:46.700
Me! Me! Me!

18:47.650 --> 18:50.230
D-Do you think I can be a hero, too?

18:50.640 --> 18:53.160
I believe... you can.

18:53.160 --> 18:55.230
I mean, even I'm a hero.

18:55.230 --> 18:56.230
You're lying!

18:57.070 --> 18:58.320
Who's that?

18:58.320 --> 19:01.420
Shy's no hero!

19:02.380 --> 19:06.120
A real hero... A real hero...

19:06.440 --> 19:09.120
wouldn't pretend to be Revozeale!

19:09.120 --> 19:11.120
<i>He actually has a point!</i>

19:11.330 --> 19:13.530
Hey, what's your problem? Shut up!

19:13.530 --> 19:16.170
What's a boy like you doing in 
the <i>Civirevo</i> section anyway?

19:16.170 --> 19:17.330
If you don't like it, leave!

19:17.330 --> 19:18.720
Don't get in our way.

19:18.720 --> 19:20.550
Yeah, leave!

19:23.680 --> 19:26.010
Okay, calm down, everyone!

19:26.010 --> 19:27.930
Let's quiet down.

19:28.340 --> 19:30.890
<i>"Shy's no hero," huh?</i>

19:31.710 --> 19:35.190
<i>I've been thinking that 
more than anyone else.</i>

19:37.150 --> 19:39.030
H-Hey there...

19:40.040 --> 19:42.360
Wh-What do you want?!

19:43.840 --> 19:48.900
I was just wondering what you meant back 
there when you said I wasn't a hero...

19:48.900 --> 19:51.900
What did I mean? Isn't it obvious?!

19:52.960 --> 19:56.920
The only hero for me is the 
one and only Revozeale!

19:57.590 --> 19:58.420
Hm?

19:58.690 --> 20:01.760
And because you're pretending to be Zeale,

20:01.760 --> 20:03.430
that means you're a fake hero!

20:03.810 --> 20:06.180
S-So you're...

20:06.560 --> 20:11.940
Wh-What? Are you also gonna tell me it's 
weird that I like <i>Civirevo</i> because I'm a boy?

20:12.350 --> 20:14.940
So what if I like it?! You jerk!

20:14.940 --> 20:16.190
Jerk?!

20:18.440 --> 20:20.440
<b>Rebel!
Civil Revolution</b>

20:21.290 --> 20:22.950
My Revozeale!

20:30.820 --> 20:31.750
Here you go.

20:33.040 --> 20:35.970
It's not good to get too obsessed...

20:35.970 --> 20:38.330
But you're able to tell 
the world what you like...

20:38.800 --> 20:42.180
And I think that's the coolest.

20:43.310 --> 20:47.510
Besides, when it comes to 
something you like or love,

20:47.510 --> 20:49.260
it doesn't matter if you're a boy or girl.

20:49.530 --> 20:51.660
Th-The thing you just said...

20:53.100 --> 20:56.600
"When it comes to something you like or love, 
it doesn't matter if you're a boy or girl!"

20:56.600 --> 20:57.180
Huh?

20:57.180 --> 21:00.140
That's exactly what Zeale said in episode 25!

21:02.020 --> 21:05.280
Y-You're real! You're the real Revozeale!

21:05.610 --> 21:06.780
Huh?

21:07.020 --> 21:09.840
N-No, I'm not! I'm Shy!

21:09.840 --> 21:12.170
I can't believe Zeale is 
right here next to me...

21:12.170 --> 21:14.260
I'm not!

21:18.210 --> 21:21.550
For some reason... I'm super tired.

21:22.600 --> 21:25.880
Wow, thank you so much for today!

21:27.070 --> 21:30.050
It's not much, but I'd like to 
give you this as thanks for today!

21:30.320 --> 21:32.040
<i>My special reward!</i>

21:32.040 --> 21:35.060
O-Oh, no... You shouldn't have...

21:35.690 --> 21:40.860
Here are the <i>Civirevo</i> 30th anniversary 
special Blu-ray box sets, just for you!

21:42.290 --> 21:42.860
Ah...

21:43.780 --> 21:45.420
Fank you...

21:49.590 --> 21:51.240
Wake up, Revoron!

21:51.730 --> 21:55.000
If we don't protect them, who will?!

21:55.000 --> 21:57.000
Revoron! Revoron!

21:57.310 --> 21:59.000
Revoron!

21:59.490 --> 22:02.000
Don't die, Revoron!

22:02.340 --> 22:04.460
Looks like you're pretty into it.
